BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 652 Tm (Likely Interview Questions and Strong Answers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 637 Tm (Q: Walk me through the architecture.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 627 Tm (A: It is a modular NestJS banking backend. REST controllers handle auth, accounts, transfers, mocks,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 617 Tm (webhooks, and health. PostgreSQL is the source of truth. Redis is used for account lookup caching.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 607 Tm (RabbitMQ decouples side effects like emails and SMS from the core transfer transaction. Brevo sends) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 597 Tm (transactional email. Docker Compose runs API, Postgres, Redis, and RabbitMQ, while Nginx exposes the API) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 587 Tm (under /finbank-api.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 572 Tm (Q: How do you ensure transfer integrity?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 562 Tm (A: Transfers run in an explicit database transaction. The service locks the two account rows with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 552 Tm (pessimistic write locks, validates status and balance, updates balances, creates one transaction record,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 542 Tm (and writes debit and credit ledger entries. If any step fails, it rolls back. Side effects like email) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 532 Tm (are published only after commit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 517 Tm (Q: Why add idempotency?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 507 Tm (A: In banking, clients retry requests because of network timeouts. Without idempotency, a retry could) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 497 Tm (debit twice. The API now accepts an idempotencyKey, stores it uniquely, and returns the original) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 487 Tm (transaction reference on replay.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 472 Tm (Q: How did you reduce deadlock risk?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 462 Tm (A: Instead of locking sender then receiver in request order, the service locks both accounts in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 452 Tm (deterministic account-number order. This avoids two concurrent opposite-direction transfers each holding) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 442 Tm (one lock and waiting on the other.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 427 Tm (Q: What did Redis do here?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 417 Tm (A: Redis caches account lookups by account number with a short TTL. After a transfer, both affected) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 407 Tm (account cache keys are invalidated so balance reads do not serve stale state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 392 Tm (Q: Why RabbitMQ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 382 Tm (A: Email and SMS are non-critical side effects. RabbitMQ lets the transfer commit quickly and reliably,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 372 Tm (then the consumer processes notifications asynchronously. It improves resilience and avoids coupling) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 362 Tm (banking consistency to an email provider outage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 347 Tm (Q: What indexes did you add and why?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 337 Tm (A: I added indexes for transaction history by source/destination account and date, status/date for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 327 Tm (operational queries, ledger account/date and reference lookup, audit user/action/date, notification) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 317 Tm (recipient/status/provider, and a unique idempotency key. These match common financial query paths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 302 Tm (Q: Why disable TypeORM synchronize in production?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 292 Tm (A: Auto-sync is convenient in development but risky in production because schema changes can happen) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 282 Tm (implicitly at startup. Financial systems should use explicit migrations or controlled SQL scripts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 267 Tm (Q: How do you handle email delivery?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 257 Tm (A: Direct Postfix was blocked on outbound port 25 and would also have SPF issues. I integrated Brevo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 247 Tm (transactional email via API, configured sender identity, and verified successful signup and transfer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 237 Tm (receipt logs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 222 Tm (Q: What would you improve next?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 212 Tm (A: Add proper TypeORM migrations, CI/CD, automated e2e tests, structured logging, metrics, tracing, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 202 Tm (real SMS provider, webhook signature verification, rate limiting, RBAC policies, reconciliation jobs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 192 Tm (settlement flows, and a secrets manager.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 177 Tm (Remaining Production Roadmap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 162 Tm (- Replace demo SQL patching with versioned TypeORM migrations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 152 Tm (- Add CI pipeline for lint, unit tests, e2e tests, and Docker build.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 142 Tm (- Add Prometheus/OpenTelemetry metrics and centralized logs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 132 Tm (- Add request correlation IDs across REST, RabbitMQ, and notification logs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 122 Tm (- Add webhook signature verification and replay protection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 112 Tm (- Add real SMS provider integration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 102 Tm (- Add admin/support authorization policies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 92 Tm (- Add reconciliation and settlement modules for complete banking operations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 82 Tm (- Move secrets to a cloud secrets manager.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 67 Tm (Interview Positioning) Tj ET
